# Fault F12 (W-A, didn't reproduce on snap6 and doesn't now): under `windows each`, a rounding axis's line wasn't split
# by window. L §4.4: `windows each` prints one line per sub-window that changes the result; an axis prints a
# line per reading (L §5.5 axis). d < e holds for d in 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-06 (1) and not after; round(0.5, 1) is
# 1 up and 0 down: four lines (the order of the lines is this interpreter's).
=== m.tally
model t11
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-15
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source src "s"
axis md
  up "up"
  down "down"
input d: date
input e: date
input f: num
def y: num = (if d < e then 1 else 0) + round(f, 1, md) at reader
ask q: y law 2026-06-30 windows each
version v
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-31) "d"
  e = 2026-03-07 "e"
  f = 0.5 "f"
=== expect
q [d = 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-06] [md = up]: 2
  reading: md = up
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-15
q [d = 2026-03-07 .. 2026-03-31] [md = up]: 1
  reading: md = up
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-15
q [d = 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-06] [md = down]: 1
  reading: md = down
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-15
q [d = 2026-03-07 .. 2026-03-31] [md = down]: 0
  reading: md = down
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-15
